    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2\\le 1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1\\le x\\le 1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-1&\\le 0\\\\(x-1)(x+1)&\\le 0\\end{align*}$$\nThe upward-opening parabola has zeroes $-1$ and $1$ and is non-positive between them, including the zeroes. Hence $-1\\le x\\le 1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2>3x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<0$ or $x>3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-3x&>0\\\\x(x-3)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe upward-opening parabola has zeroes $0$ and $3$ and is positive outside these zeroes. Hence $x<0$ or $x>3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^2\\ge 144$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le -12$ or $x\\ge 12$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-144&\\ge 0\\\\(x-12)(x+12)&\\ge 0\\end{align*}$$\nThe upward-opening parabola has zeroes $-12$ and $12$ and is non-negative outside them, including the zeroes. Hence $x\\le -12$ or $x\\ge 12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^2>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\ne 0$",
          "worked": "The parabola $y=x^2$ touches the $x$-axis at $x=0$ and is above it everywhere else. Hence $x<0$ or $x>0$, equivalently $x\\ne 0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^2+9\\le 6x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-6x+9&\\le 0\\\\(x-3)^2&\\le 0\\end{align*}$$\nA square is non-negative, so it is non-positive only when it equals zero. Thus $x-3=0$, giving $x=3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$4x-3\\ge x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1\\le x\\le 3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4x+3&\\le 0\\\\(x-1)(x-3)&\\le 0\\end{align*}$$\nThe upward-opening parabola has zeroes $1$ and $3$ and is non-positive between them, including the zeroes. Hence $1\\le x\\le 3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
